      explanation: `<div style="--mx-navy:#01506e; --mx-blue:#207bb5; --mx-lightblue:#0099d4; --mx-yellow:#e9dc12; --mx-grey:#4B556A; --mx-rule:#dde4ea; --mx-tint:#f2f7fa; --mx-body:#232a33; color:var(--mx-body); line-height:1.6"><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-yellow); padding:13px 18px; margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">A. $58,400 is correct.</strong> The bank balance needs only the two items the bank has not processed yet: deposits in transit and outstanding checks.</div><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The rule</h3><p style="margin:0 0 12px">A reconciliation runs <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">two columns</strong>. The bank column starts with the statement balance and adjusts for items the bank has not seen: <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">add deposits in transit</strong> and <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">subtract outstanding checks</strong>. The book column starts with the ledger balance and adjusts for items the company has not recorded: service charges, NSF checks and its own recording errors. Both columns must land on the same <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">adjusted cash balance</strong>, and that figure is the cash reported on the balance sheet.</p><p style="margin:0 0 18px">The trap is the other three items. The $20 service charge, the $700 NSF check and the $45 deposit error are <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">already inside the $60,000</strong>, because the bank handled each one correctly. Pulling them out of the bank column double counts them. They are <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">book side</strong> adjustments only.</p><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The math</h3><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-blue); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:18px"><table style="border:0; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Balance per bank statement</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$60,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Add: deposits in transit</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">400</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Less: outstanding checks</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">(2,000)</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Adjusted cash balance</strong></td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">$58,400</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The book side entry</h3><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-blue); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:18px"><table style="border:0; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Account</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Debit</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Credit</strong></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Cash, deposit recorded $45 too low</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$45</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Accounts receivable, NSF check</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">700</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Bank service charge expense</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">20</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px 11px 40px">Accounts receivable, deposit error</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$45</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px 11px 40px">Cash, NSF and service charge</td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">720</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="margin:0 0 12px">Cash falls a <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">net $675</strong> on the books, so the ledger balance of $59,075 also reconciles to <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">$58,400</strong>. Bank side items need no entry: the bank corrects itself when the deposit posts and the checks clear.</p></div>`,
